[{:task "seon.turn/observe-reads-are-renders" :merge "fb541052f" :plan-at "merge" :plan "Owner, 2026-10-27 (approved direction, via root): \"I want the eval system to stay rock solid and for it to be focused on executing code and instrumenting it ... Info that is derived and made for the agent or the user should go into the hiccup ... The whole web rendering only what's changed seems like an opportunity to make expensive ops mostly cheap as you only pay them once.\" What exists: seon.turn/observe (turn.clj) runs every turn: agent/prove! (a blocking test run), added-gaps, branch/unmerged, problems/caused-split, task/task, agent/merge-readiness (99% of a turn: 1.78B ticks with main moved, from seon.merge/touched-keys over main's whole diff), program/divergence and the done rule; basis! stores :observed (results, reasons, will-merge, merge) in :seon.turn/basis (derived data in the db, against the 2026-10-26 ruling), observed! holds it in agent state for my.task/status; run-tests-forked's parent waits for its child (agent.clj, read-to-exit) on the agent's one thread; test-plan reads stored-results on the branch db, where results never land (they land on main). The experiment (root's scratchpad render-not-eval.md, forms 01-16) measured them as renders: nothing moved 108 ticks, an unrelated eval 8K ticks with nothing re-run, main moving re-runs only merge-view; a render's cached output equals a fresh call. Build: (1) seon.render.ui components declaring :seon.db/db, each with main's and base's t (ctx's environment :main-t :base-t, ctx-atom's) as children: merge-view (delta-three-way; child divergence's value until datoms-diff's reads are in its read set), caused-view (caused-split), tests-view (the plan's selection, main's results at its digests, an unrun test shown running), gaps-view (added-gaps), divergence-view; placed in render-ctx's task list beside status. (2) seon.turn/observe keeps only the done rule's inputs, called directly (the judge and hand-back! call the same functions at the run's end); merge-readiness, divergence, :attention, :tests, :reds and the prove! wait leave the turn; basis! stores no :observed; observed!/input become a read of the page and my.task/status reads it. (3) each eval's commit sends one non-blocking :prove; tests-view shows its results from main. (4) (fork f) -> value, its answer a message, never a wait; run-tests-forked its caller. (5) test-plan reads results from main. Deletes: observed, :seon.turn/basis's :observed, the prove! wait in observe, merge-readiness per turn. Proofs: an unrelated eval re-runs none of these renders (ledger :hit, a frame under 10K ticks); a main move re-runs merge-view once; the cached output equals a fresh call; a turn's observe under 15M ticks with main moved (1.78B today); the judge's verdict unchanged on the e2e checks. Owner: agent view (this session), turn.clj and agent.clj's test-run parts by root's go; ctx-atom adds :main-commit and :base-commit. Phase A (this branch): (1) less tests-view and (2); the tests view waits on phase B, (3)-(5), which gives it a producer." :fns ["my.agent/deferred" "my.task/status" "seon.agent/heard-main" "seon.agent/merge-main!" "seon.agent/run-tests-forked" "seon.agent/test-plan" "seon.context/turn-state" "seon.merge/readiness" "seon.render.ui/caused-view" "seon.render.ui/commit-db" "seon.render.ui/divergence-view" "seon.render.ui/gaps-view" "seon.render.ui/merge-view" "seon.render.ui/render-ctx" "seon.turn/observe" "seon.turn/observed"] :sections ["docs/agent.md#what-you-read" "docs/health.md#a-stale-section" "docs/health.md#what-a-branch-caused" "docs/merging.md#a-merge-runs-what-the-change-reaches" "docs/turn.md#observe"] :schemas [] :tasks ["seon.context/the-turn-shows-what-will-merge" "seon.turn/the-fork-server-hands-main-s-index"]}
