{:task "seon.proofs/main-is-proved-in-a-fork" :merge "858af0505" :plan-at "parent" :plan "Owner, 2026-10-27: \"We should be able to cheaply (ms) fork main and run main tests and update the shared test knowledge base for all agents.\" What existed: `seon.prove`'s :main input (the writer's commit notice) only kept main's t, so main was proved only when someone asked (a session's seon_prove, root's gate), and an agent forked from main found none of main's results; a main run spawned a prove agent that then read, load-string'ed and imported every test file of the checkout (`seon.agent/load-tests!`, about 2.2 s + 5.4 s cold for src and test, scratchpad tests-fast.md section 6), though the fork server's main already holds the tests (:seon.config.source/dirs takes test/), and main's run was keyed by the checkout's inputs too (`seon.root/prove!` read the tree through the :source effect). Done: a notice whose ops move the program (`seon.program/moves-program?`, moved here from seon.fork-server, which uses it too) is a request to prove main keyed by its program digest, with no waiter, joined by any session asking for that key; the prove agent forked from main runs at once (the :prepare step deleted); main's key is its program digest as an agent's is. Results are the result-tx facts on main every agent forked after reads (`seon.proofs/stored-results`). Deletes `seon.agent/load-tests!`, `seon.prove/read-digest`, root/prove!'s :source read, and the answer's `:ran true` that hid the run's own :ran count. Not done: digests equal across bin/test and an agent's run (the reuse session's work); process tests stay with bin/prove --merge." :fns ["seon.agent/run-tests-forked" "seon.prove/answered"] :sections [] :schemas [] :tasks []}
