{:task "datahike.db/a-diff-records-its-reads" :merge "70b488af2" :plan-at "merge" :plan "Found by root's render-not-eval experiment, 2026-10-27 (blocker 1): d/datoms-diff (reference-code/datahike/src/datahike/db.cljc, datoms-diff) reaches psi/diff past the index protocol (datahike.index.interface), whose -slice, -rslice, -lookup and -count-slice record each range under d/with-reads (di/record-read!), so a read built on a diff recorded nothing: a render over a diff (merge readiness as a render) was skipped after its branch added a program key, keeping its old answer. Fix in the fork (jolt/a-diff-records-its-reads, 65dad766): psi/diff records its [from to] range as -slice does, so the read's key is the diffed attribute ([:a a]) or :any, and seon.render's walk matches a transaction against it like any read (render!, frame!). Coarse by design: any datom in the diffed range touches it, as a slice's does. Replaces nothing; the alternative, a render passing the diff's inputs as its children, is a second way to say what it read. Seen on the way: task a-diff-equals-the-set-difference-on-every-history." :fns [] :sections ["docs/forks.md#datahike" "docs/forks.md#jolt"] :schemas [] :tasks ["datahike.db/a-diff-equals-the-set-difference-on-every-history" "datahike.db/a-time-predicate-read-keeps-index-order" "datahike.transaction/a-replaced-value-is-retracted-in-the-report" "datahike.transaction/an-index-insert-allocates-nothing-extra" "jolt.backend/a-deftype-method-call-takes-a-site-cache" "jolt.backend/a-try-entered-allocates-nothing" "jolt.backend/build-smoke-is-green-on-the-pin"]}
{:task "seon.reconcile/the-index-is-checked-once" :merge "a39ebb7d7" :plan-at "merge" :plan "Every reconciler helper (put-task, derive-needs, refresh-ready, refresh-done, idx-ready?, done-info, ...) takes `:seon.reconcile/index`, and its contract checked every entry of the index's map-of and set parts on each call, so listing the index (```seon.reconcile/index``` of a db, an agent's first request build through seon.turn's index!) cost tasks x tasks. Measured on a worktree root's main of 903 tasks: 156M ticks and 636 MB with the contracts on, 26.8M and 149 MB off. The index's parts are checked by kind (:map, set?), and each entry where it enters (put-task's :seon.task/own, put-run's :seon.run/run), as :seon.ctx/ix already was ([cost](docs/cost.md#what-a-contract-costs)): 33.0M ticks and 160 MB after. The `*` pull of a task (seon.task/entity-value) was not a cause: it costs 16k ticks and 90 KB a task, against 41k and 165 KB for a pull naming :seon.task/own's 15 attributes, so it stays." :fns [] :sections ["docs/cost.md#what-a-contract-costs"] :schemas [":seon.reconcile/index" ":seon.reconcile/state"] :tasks ["seon.reconcile/a-work-task-merges-itself-through-the-one-gate"]}
