{:task "datahike.transaction/an-index-insert-allocates-nothing-extra" :merge "a37057eb8" :plan-at "merge" :plan "Found by root's perf pass, 2026-10-27 (perf-2026-10-27.md): d/db-with of the boot import (~125k datoms) costs 1,914M ticks and 4.88 GB against an estimated need of 350-600M ticks and 50-250 MB. Measured (worktree session an-index-insert-allocates-nothing-extra, seon.profile/measure!): keyword compare (cmp-attr-quick) is not it, 6 ticks and 0 B. One transient :eavt insert is 2.2k ticks and 2.86 KB, 13 comparisons a descent; per comparison, Jolt's == in combine-cmp 32 B (jolt-num-equiv, a rest-args procedure called through its var) and, when e and a match, Datahike's Jolt compare-value 240 B (a try entered, 176 B, and two letfn closures). Fixed at both producers: Jolt jolt/num-equiv-two-args (a 2-arity, 0 B; make numequivalloc) and Datahike jolt/compare-value-no-try (two values of one scalar kind compare with no try). What stays: every interop call on a deftype (.lookup, .cons, .root) walks the method arms with no site cache (task jolt.backend/a-deftype-method-call-takes-a-site-cache), and the import's larger owners are outside the insert: per entity a content id's hash 43 KB (hasch), an identity's upsert ~16 KB, an entity map's expansion ~10 KB (task an-identity-costs-its-seek)." :fns [] :sections ["docs/forks.md#datahike" "docs/forks.md#jolt"] :schemas [] :tasks ["datahike.transaction/a-replaced-value-is-retracted-in-the-report" "jolt.backend/a-deftype-method-call-takes-a-site-cache" "jolt.backend/a-try-entered-allocates-nothing" "jolt.backend/build-smoke-is-green-on-the-pin"]}
