{:task "seon.proofs/a-failed-import-leaves-no-branch" :merge "c766038ba" :plan-at "parent" :plan "Found by form-keywords, 2026-10-25: test-runner/program-db makes the tree's branch (d/branch!) before it transacts that tree's import, so when the transact fails (here Datahike refused a :form/keywords value: datahike.transaction/a-keyword-attributes-two-values-are-two-values), the branch stays, named for the tree, empty or behind. The next plan of a changed tree branches from it as the kept tree of the fewest changed files and refreshes only those, so its program db holds only the namespaces changed since: `bin/test seon.program-test` selected 0 tests and said TEST OK, and datahike.query-test, untouched, selected 0. Fix at the producer: the branch exists only once its import committed (transact on a branch named for the tree only after, or delete the branch when the transact throws, as the one edge function the failure-points page names). Proof: a plan whose import throws leaves the store's branches as they were, and the next plan of the same program finds every test namespace." :fns [] :sections ["docs/source.md#tests-run-by-reach"] :schemas [] :tasks []}
{:task "seon.source/a-tests-reach-is-the-same-however-the-program-was-analyzed" :merge "634f18ab5" :plan-at "parent" :plan "A test's class (process or not, seon.program/graph-index's :process?) and its digest depend on how the program db was built, not only on the program. Three observations. (1) Agent view: seon.source records a quoted name ((list 'seon.turn/work! ...) in seon.reconcile/advance) as a reach edge only when the named namespace was analyzed first, so 10 reconciler tests were process tests on one branch and not on main; hidden by building the symbol by name (4c7fd7800, the same trick as seon.render.ui/did). (2) Agent loop: calling seon.task/session-key twice in the reconciler's step moved 9 reconciler tests, seon.procs-test/reconciler and seon.problems-test/a-defect-in-the-reconciler-does-not-feed-itself into left out (241 -> 251); either call alone does not; reproduce from jolt/agent-loop's history, the commit before 0c2fa6434. (3) Measured on main d79bee61e (worktree reds-the-full-run-found): the same tree's plan (bin/test --plan both) on its kept program store, a branch refreshed from the nearest kept tree (test-runner/program-db, seon.source/refresh-tx), leaves out 240 (496 keys); on a fresh store (seon.source/import-tx of the whole tree) 250 (486 keys); the refreshed set is a strict subset (the 10 are 8 seon.reconcile-test, 1 seon.procs-test, 1 seon.problems-test). The branch's tree refreshed leaves out 188 (549 keys), fresh 251: refresh dropped 63 process edges. So keys and digests differ for one tree, which also breaks reuse by digest. Correct: the analysis gives the same facts and edges whatever the order and however many times a name appears, and an incremental refresh gives what a whole import gives (seon.program/reach-update's own rule: an update gives the digests a rebuild gives); the rule for a quoted name in a form (a call or not) is stated once (docs/references.md or the program page) and applied the same everywhere. Then the symbol-build