{:task "seon.proofs/one-prove-path" :merge "f83b736e1" :plan-at "merge" :plan "Owner, 2026-10-25 (docs/decisions.md, root's special cases go: one prove path). What existed: a proof run's tick budget was per run, two keys by mode (`:seon.config.agent/test-ticks` for the judge, a turn's own 10x smaller one), so a test's verdict depended on where it ran and on what ran before it in the run: a proof that needed more than the turn's budget was red (`:seon.test/ticks-spent` on the running test) in every turn and green at the judge, and a cheap test after a costly one was red in one run and green alone. bin/test had no bound at all, and its greens are reused by digest by agents. And the judge forked a child even when every test it selected was green at its digest (what the turn had just run). Changed: `seon.proofs/run-tests!` (the one runner) takes a per-test bound: each test, its :each fixtures included, runs under a Jolt `run-interruptible` budget of its own inside its :each fixtures (so their teardown runs), the namespace's fixtures within the tests' budgets and one more (`seon.proofs/test-vars`, Jolt's clojure.test fixture atoms); a test past it is an `:error` report of `:seon.test/ticks-spent` naming it and the run goes on; each result records its `:ticks`. One key, `:seon.config.agent/test-ticks` (200e9, the old judge bound), per test, used by a turn, the judge and bin/test (test/test_runner.clj); 0 means none, read once in the runner. `seon.agent/run-tests-forked` forks nothing when nothing is left to run. Deleted: the turn's own key (config, two schema entries), the mode switch in `seon.agent/handle!`, `seon.agent/run-tests-here`'s run-level budget and its error assembly. Kept by ruling (a), 2026-10-22: what a turn selects (proofs and what the branch changed) and what the judge selects (the plan); the judge runs the plan less every green at its digest, so after a turn it runs only what the turn did not. Not changed: reds are not reused (a red reruns, to the same verdict now that the bound is the test's own); the judge still asks the agent's `:tests` op rather than `seon.prove` (its runs are not recorded on main as the turn's are). Correctness: one verdict per test and digest everywhere. Perf: a judge after a covering turn forks no child and runs no test (measured in seon.agent-test/one-bound-one-verdict-and-the-judge-reruns-no-green: :ran 0, no :pid); a turn may now do up to the per-test bound per selected test (its selection is the proofs and what changed)." :fns ["seon.agent/handle!" "seon.agent/run-tests-forked" "seon.agent/run-tests-here" "seon.agent/test-report" "seon.proofs/run-tests!" "seon.proofs/test-vars" "seon.root/run-tests!"] :sections ["docs/failure-points.md#edges-that-catch-each-names-its-one-variant" "docs/failure-points.md#entrant-boundaries-a-defect-becomes-a-recorded-error-map" "docs/failure-points.md#failure-points-met-without-a-catch-the-edge-answers-data" "docs/merging.md#a-merge-runs-what-the-change-reaches" "docs/processes.md#the-agent-process" "docs/turn.md#observe" "docs/turn.md#who-runs-which-tests"] :schemas [":seon.config.agent/test-ticks"] :tasks ["seon.proofs/a-prove-runs-key-does-not-move-between-two-asks"]}
