{:task "seon.cost/a-cost-proof-is-the-same-under-load" :merge "205b0dc41" :plan-at "parent" :plan "Reproduction: Found 2026-10-23 by the cutover's decider: red in a built scratch worktree of main 4bc598dc1 as well as in the fresh clone, so it is main's, not the cutover's. In a loaded 4-shard `bin/test --all` (load average about 12) `seon.vector-cost-test/a-search-reads-each-row-once` (bytes grew as n^1.96, linear allows n^1.88; per-n ratios 1.04, 1.02, 1.00) and `seon.program-cost-test/a-probed-entity-is-sought-not-scanned` (ticks n^0.62, log allows n^0.60; ratios 0.89-0.94) went red; run alone, each is green in the same tree and in main. AGENTS section 5 says ticks and bytes are exact and the same on any machine, so a number that moves with load is measuring something else (bytes allocated by a concurrent thread? a GC in the window?). Find what moves and exclude it from the count, or widen the fit's tolerance on the exponent with the measured spread (cost-tolerances-are-derived). Replaces nothing." :fns [] :sections ["docs/cost.md#what-is-measured"] :schemas [] :tasks []}
