{:task "jolt.backend/image-registration-is-opt-in" :merge "9bda779cd" :plan-at "parent" :plan "Done (worktree session reuse, 2026-10-23; Jolt jolt/image-fn-forms-opt-in 686aff7d, eba8826a). Jolt registers every fn literal's source for its state image: fnsrc-flush renders the source, reads it back to check it (fnsrc-row-src), emits image-register-fn-form! per literal and wraps the literal in a maker. Seon writes no image. Now an explicit Jolt compile option, not a changed default: *compiler-options* {:image-fn-forms false} makes a top-level form collect no registrations (backend_scheme.clj fnsrc-regs answers nil), its literals emitted as plain closures with their names; absent or true, Jolt is unchanged for every other user. Jolt reads JOLT_COMPILER_OPTIONS (an EDN map) into *compiler-options*' root at start (post-prelude.ss), as JVM Clojure reads the clojure.compiler.* properties, and Seon sets it in bin/env, so its build, the test runner, root and the agents it forks all compile without registration. Measured: a realistic defn with four literals 5.14 -> 3.47 MB (-33%); a defn of n literals ~1.24 MB and ~172k ticks a literal registering, ~478 KB and ~52k not (-62%, -68%). Known: JOLT_COMPILER_OPTIONS is no input of a test's reach digest (bin/env fixes it), and Jolt's AOT cache keys a namespace without it, so a unit compiled with registration may be loaded without it and the reverse (harmless to Seon, which writes no image)." :fns [] :sections ["docs/forks.md#jolt" "docs/source.md#shared-build-caches"] :schemas [":seon.config.build/jolt-compiler-options"] :tasks []}
{:task "seon.watch/a-vanished-file-is-a-fact" :merge "78e998765" :plan-at "merge" :plan "Found 2026-10-23: the standing root's watcher died, seon.watch/died: its batch handler threw .../docs/references.md (No such file or directory): root no longer watches the checkout (exit 143). A git merge or bin/update removed the file for a moment while the batch read the wiki: seon.docs/pages listed docs/ and then slurped each file, and the one gone in between threw. Correct, at the producer (root's ruling): one read of a directory's files, seon.lib/dir-texts, which seon.docs/pages and my.root/task-files both call, leaves out a file listed and gone when read, as a deleted file is: the wiki's load retracts that page's sections, a task file left out is not judged (seon.task/load-tx: a file not given is not judged, so its tasks are never cancelled by a moment's absence), and the change that removed it or writes it back makes the next batch. The catch is FileNotFoundException only, named in docs/failure-points.md. Folds the two directory readers the one-offs survey found (notes/one-offs-2026-10-23.md, item 6)." :fns ["my.root/task-files" "seon.docs/pages" "seon.lib/dir-texts"] :sections ["docs/failure-points.md#edges-that-catch-each-names-its-one-variant"] :schemas [] :tasks []}
