{:task "seon.root/the-api-uses-flows-own-channels" :merge "2156f548b" :plan-at "parent" :plan "What exists: (1) `seon.root/start!` starts a thread, seon-flow-errors, that alts!! on one channel (Flow's error chan) and puts each defect on :back as {:op :error :pid :message :data :msg}; `seon.root/stop!` joins it with .join 5000; `seon.check/threads` declares it. (2) The api's step collects outputs in its state (::to-agents, ::replies; root.clj:119, :173) and flushes them through `seon.step/out!` at the step's end (:533-536), beside the step's own outputs volatile. Correct: (1) (a/pipe error-chan (a/chan 1 (map ->op)) ...) into :back: no thread, no join; (2) each site calls `seon.step/out!` on o, as `seon.root/back-op` already does. Deletes the thread, its join and roster entry, the two state keys and the flush. A failure point: \u00a75 allows a thread only for a blocking foreign read." :fns ["seon.root/answer-spawn" "seon.root/answer-taken" "seon.root/api-one" "seon.root/api-proc" "seon.root/back-op" "seon.root/deliver-message" "seon.root/deliver-rid" "seon.root/end-agent" "seon.root/ext-op" "seon.root/record-death" "seon.root/reply!" "seon.root/set-agent" "seon.root/spawn-failed" "seon.root/start!" "seon.root/stop!" "seon.root/to-agent"] :sections ["docs/failure-points.md#entrant-boundaries-a-defect-becomes-a-recorded-error-map" "docs/flow.md#idioms-for-seon"] :schemas [] :tasks []}
{:task "seon.test-store/a-kept-store-is-keyed-by-its-schema" :merge "1f19114c1" :plan-at "merge" :plan "Found 2026-10-23 by root: the page merge changed three attributes to refs, and every checkout's kept target/program-store and target/runs/test-store refused to open (seon.db/open!: :seon.db/types-differ, another value type than the schema declares). bin/test failed at its plan, and process tests at root start. Both are regenerable output, made again from their inputs, never records. Fix: seon.db/schema-digest names the schema; seon.test-store/kept-store! answers base-<digest> and removes a store at base of another schema (base itself, or base-<8 hex digits>), sparing a runs directory beside it. The test runner's program store and the process store (seon.test-store/process-store, made by the plan's seon.test-store/make-process-store!, which replaces bin/test's seed step) are named by it. A changed schema makes a new store; nothing is migrated or refused." :fns ["seon.db/schema-digest"] :sections ["docs/merging.md#a-merge-runs-what-the-change-reaches"] :schemas [] :tasks ["seon.test-store/a-test-root-is-its-own"]}
