{:task "seon.render/page" :merge "5666aebb3" :plan-at "parent" :plan "Every page is the walk of one entity (seon.render/walk) through its :html face (owner, 2026-10-23: \"no separate run view it's part of the agents view\"; \"root is also an agents view, it just has different focus since it should be linked up with all the agents it's running on the system, the system health, etc\"). What exists: seon.render.proc/zoom-value assembles an agent's window by hand from root's view, main's run and the branch, joined by strings (turn-rows, eval-records, a tile list, a run-or-agent branch, a :turn-ctx cache), the /run/{id} route beside /agent/{id}, and root's page a second producer (seon.render.ui/system-page, agent-card and the grid). Build: a location is an entity (/agent/{id} resolves to the agent's eid in root's boot, / to root's); the page is the walk: the entity as the main pane (:block), its units the column (:tile) in their declared order, each a link that moves the eid; a unit is rendered again when a commit changes its entity (the render proc's events), never polled. The owner's window is the same evaluations the model's context shows (seon.context/evaluations), through the :html face: one list, newest at the top, each evaluation rendered once (its thought, its form, its result by the result's own render, its cost), a model turn grouping its evaluations under its header; no second output (no transcript beside a column of the same results), and no special place for now: it is the newest evaluation (owner, 2026-10-23: \"I'm wondering if we don't just limit it to now and instead it's every eval that renders to html sorted by newest at the top\"; \"no I don't want separate outputs I want responsive html and css so why not tailwind?\"). Layout is responsive CSS: a render tags its root with how it is shown (:as) and Tailwind's classes lay it out at each width; the content a render includes is its own choice by :as (an :inline value is one line, for the :ai face too). Tailwind as v1 built it, ported to Jolt's build (owner, 2026-10-23: \"look at the ~/src/seon I think we had something for tailwind generation? but build it for the jolt build process so it's simple and we can just update the css and it regenerrates without a lot of fuss\"): v1's ~/src/seon/bin/css is a two-argument transform, Tailwind v4 CSS-first (every directive, token and source glob in resources/public/css/input.css, no config file), measured 171-187 ms, a build product and never a runtime component (v1 deleted its Integrant watcher). Keep v1's lessons: `@import \"tailwindcss\" source(none)` with explicit `@source` globs over src/**/*.clj (auto-detection walked the reference-code tree: 42 s, against ~1 s), and a safelist of the utility vocabulary agents may use, since a render an agent defines at its REPL is never in a scanned file. On Jolt: Tailwind's standalone v4 binary in place of bun and node_modules, pinned by version and checksum, fetched into target/ and run as a step of bin/build (and so of the :build effect after merges), its output reused by the digest of input.css and the scanned sources (AGENTS \u00a75): edit input.css or a render's classes, build, and the stylesheet is regenerated; unchanged inputs regenerate nothing. The hand-written app.css goes. The chat input (evaluate, message, interrupt, release) stays at the top, where the newest is. Only what is on screen is rendered (owner, 2026-10-23: \"We can dynamically load the tiles and not show the ones offscreen right?\"): the page carries the newest units and a placeholder saying how many older there are; when it scrolls into view (Datastar's data-on-intersect) the render proc renders the next ones, so the server works only for what is looked at, by that event, never a poll. Deletes zoom-value, turn-rows, eval-records' joins, the /run route, system-page's hand-built sections, agent-card and the grid (one :tile render of an agent replaces both), the tile list and :turn-ctx. A browser subagent compares each page against the facts (notes/browser-tester.md). The old window's last browser round (2026-10-23, agent a5) found what the new page must not repeat: a count of evaluations the list does not show (every evaluation is a row, or the count is not shown); a name shortened without saying so (the branch's :main/ prefix); a tile that says 0 without saying nothing has run; numbers without their unit or label, and a warning without its bound." :fns ["seon.render.ai/section-load" "seon.render.proc/answered" "seon.render.proc/ask-branches" "seon.render.proc/boot-of" "seon.render.proc/finish-patch" "seon.render.proc/history-cap" "seon.render.proc/location" "seon.render.proc/main-info" "seon.render.proc/on-event" "seon.render.proc/page-value" "seon.render.proc/pass" "seon.render.proc/pass-view" "seon.render.proc/ready?" "seon.render.proc/render-proc" "seon.render.proc/render-unit" "seon.render.proc/step-units" "seon.render.proc/system-value" "seon.render.proc/this-boots" "seon.render.ui/agent-input" "seon.render.ui/asked-by" "seon.render.ui/context-read?" "seon.render.ui/cost-line" "seon.render.ui/error-box" "seon.render.ui/evaluation" "seon.render.ui/event-detail" "seon.render.ui/head" "seon.render.ui/load-tiles" "seon.render.ui/message" "seon.render.ui/more" "seon.render.ui/page" "seon.render.ui/root-input" "seon.render.ui/row" "seon.render.ui/rows" "seon.render.ui/run-row" "seon.render.ui/shell" "seon.render.ui/shown-as" "seon.render.ui/shown-status" "seon.render.ui/thought" "seon.render.ui/tile" "seon.render.ui/turn" "seon.render.ui/view-param" "seon.render/merged" "seon.render/page" "seon.render/shown" "seon.web/handler" "seon.web/http-in" "seon.web/page-doc" "seon.web/public-dir" "seon.web/stylesheet" "seon.web/view-of"] :sections ["docs/dashboard.md#the-dashboard" "docs/dashboard.md#the-render-proc" "docs/dashboard.md#the-web-proc" "docs/failure-points.md#failure-points-met-without-a-catch-the-edge-answers-data" "docs/parity.md#context-printing-the-page" "docs/rende