0k tokens, ~$0.004; - #9: 7 turns, 54k tokens, ~$0.002. The model saw every result (the tool messages hold the sources), so this is not missing context. Task seon.turn/a-turn-shows-its-cost-against-its-budget: the turn profile's spans and the timing audit's gaps (eval ticks/CPU, the turn's split shown against an estimate, the fork server's replay, spawn and merges recorded as facts)" :fns ["seon.template/instructions"] :sections [] :schemas [] :tasks ["seon.context/the-map-reads-the-program-not-the-process" "seon.context/the-state-names-what-was-read" "seon.problems/an-observers-defect-is-a-problem-not-a-refusal"]}
{:task "commits/calc-stop" :merge "9776fc87e" :plan-at "commits" :plan "Root answers :seon.root/ended for a request to an agent that ended; prove reads that type (root's review: the fix at the producer, not the reader). - seon.root/absent (over the agent's view entry) is the one answer for an agent that is not there: :seon.root/ended when the view records its :ended-ms (a kill, its attempt's end, a death), :seon.root/no-agent when root never had it. Used by the api (:eval :tests :stats :merge-tests :merge-main, :clone's parent), request's merge-main! and prove!. - end-agent answers its in-flight requests :seon.root/ended. - seon.prove/finish does not record :seon.root/ended as a :platform problem (the agent's end is its attempt's record), with no id comparison and no guard. - The reconciler's :spawned answer takes :seon.root/ended as the agent's end. - Docs: root.md, failure-points.md. Proofs: - seon.procs-test/an-agent-that-ended-is-answered-ended-one-never-had-no-agent (the producer: every op, the clone, an in-flight request, request's merge-main!); - seon.prove-test/a-run-whose-agent-ended-is-answered-not-a-platform-problem. bin/check e2e-calc: E2E OK (red on main c32ca315). Self-review: 7 findings, all fixed. A prove run whose own agent ended is answered, not recorded as a :platform problem (bin/check e2e-calc's red on main c32ca315). The scenario cancels a task: its agent is killed while its turn's prove request is running on it, the api answers :seon.root/no-agent naming that agent, and seon.prove/finish recorded every error as a :platform problem. The scenario's quiet! then read a defect and failed, and repeated on a rerun. The agent's end is its attempt's record (:killed); the run that asked it ends with it. Any other error (another agent gone, a failed run) is recorded as before. Proof: seon.prove-test/a-run-whose-agent-ended-is-answered-not-a-platform-problem (answered, nothing recorded, nothing remembered; another agent's absence still recorded). bin/check e2e-calc: E2E OK (red before). Not this change: seon.prove-test's a-session-prove-of-main-runs-in-a-prove-agent-and-leaves-facts and a-session-and-an-agents-turn-for-one-digest-end-in-one-run fail here as their own root fails to boot (\"Could not locate seon/render/proc.jolt ... on the source roots\")." :fns ["seon.prove/finish" "seon.reconcile/advance" "seon.reconcile/dead-tx" "seon.root/absent" "seon.root/end-agent" "seon.root/ended" "seon.root/ext-op" "seon.root/prove!" "seon.root/request"] :sections ["docs/failure-points.md#edges-that-catch-each-names-its-one-variant" "docs/root.md#holders-and-refused-spawns"] :schemas [":seon.root/ended" ":seon.root/no-agent"] :tasks []}
