ded. Task seon.reconcile/a-refused-attempt-is-held-for-root (owner, 2026-10-23: \"no automatic retries, send it to root to decide if it should be retried\"): its plan, its five proofs; it replaces a-failure-attaches-a-refinement, stuck-is-observed-data and a-merged-fix-retries-what-it-failed (an automatic retry); seon.main/drivers-leave-src needs it instead. A continued branch takes its refinement's tasks from main: seon.task/onto-tx puts the task and the tasks it needs that the branch lacks onto it, and seon.agent/init! writes it for a resumed branch (the agent owns its branch's writes). Step E's run 2: both refinements, continuing the failed design's branch, read their task as nil and threw (seon.reconcile/dials). seon.task-test/a-continued-branch-takes-its-refinements-tasks-from-main." :fns ["my.root/run!" "seon.agent/init!" "seon.e2e/held" "seon.e2e/held-as" "seon.e2e/merge-counts" "seon.e2e/run" "seon.e2e/scenario" "seon.e2e/swarm" "seon.fixtures/scenarios" "seon.problems/answers" "seon.problems/failed-row" "seon.problems/report" "seon.problems/task-done?" "seon.proofs/check-steps" "seon.reconcile/actions" "seon.reconcile/advance" "seon.reconcile/evidence" "seon.reconcile/hold-tx" "seon.reconcile/idx-ready?" "seon.reconcile/judge-tx" "seon.reconcile/start" "seon.reconcile/stuck" "seon.render.ai/problem-row" "seon.render.ai/report" "seon.render.ai/task" "seon.render.ai/task-shown" "seon.render.ui/task-box" "seon.server/task-summaries" "seon.task/carry-tx" "seon.task/onto-tx" "seon.task/stated-attributes" "seon.template/request"] :sections ["docs/agent.md#done" "docs/agent.md#ending" "docs/agent.md#what-you-read" "docs/parity.md#the-agents-repl-my" "docs/tasks.md#a-refused-attempt-is-held-for-root" "docs/tasks.md#a-request-is-one-transaction" "docs/vocabulary.md#tasks-task-chains-words-worktree-sessions-r1-and-m1"] :schemas [":seon.attempt/status" ":seon.config.merge/max-merge-turns" ":seon.problems/class" ":seon.reconcile/action" ":seon.reconcile/merge-limits" "